  "proof_checks": [
    "The actual order9/order3 normalizers centralize the adjacent cubic action, and their commutator forces that action trivial on the cyclic group-ring module at every level.",
    "The norm-polynomial annihilation on the actual six-prime subgroup makes the full B2 ordinary class action trivial; the ambiguous class number and genus map then give the complete group and all27 principality decisions.",
    "Both inclusions identify the two S-split Hilbert class fields; Hilbert94 and the explicit valuation obstruction force every original S-class group to have exponent3.",
    "The exact lower genus map uses40 literal norm determinants and certified degree6 arithmetic; its degree and the known original prime order give the full L2 ordinary group.",
    "All ordinary norm and extension matrices are computed on actual Frobenius primes with inverse coordinates; the prime7 transport uses the proved trivial class action.",
    "The norm-one divisor construction gives both Hilbert90 quotient maps, their independence of choices, their exact kernels and surjectivity.",
    "The S-unit Herbrand quotients use the actual local degrees, and the killed-degree extension splits by lifting the five free finite-module generators.",
    "All completion maps are on finitely generated groups; roots-of-unity kernels, free ranks, finite norm images and every nonempty fibre are retained."
  ],
  "scope": "E.86 evaluates both entire S-class towers in actual coherent prime bases: Cl_S(B_d){3}=C3 and Cl_S(L_d){3}=C3^2, with all adjacent norm matrices identity and all extension matrices zero. The B2 and L2 ordinary three-class groups are C9+C3^2 and C9+C3, with full genus restriction, inverse Smith, ordinary norm and extension maps. All27 E81 ideals are principal and the full B2 principal S-divisor lattice has index27. The cyclic cubic/ninth B-unit defects are C3, with full norm quotient C_(3^r)^5+C3; the adjacent original L-unit defect is C3^2, with full norm quotient C3^3. Explicit Hilbert90 maps and every finite completed norm fibre are proved. Higher ordinary prime3 orders and eventual exponent h, the particular xi*c1 norm coset, and the remaining global and intrinsic section questions stay active.",
